To sign your kernel image (Image) manually, make use of install_image_imx8.sh script

1. Build your kernel image normally.

1.1 Fetch the kernel source

# git clone https://github.com/ADLINK/linux.git -b lf-6.6.y/sp2-imx8mp

1.2 build kernel image

# make adlink_sp2imx8mp_defconfig
# make

After successful build, the unsigned kernel image is located at arch/arm64/boot/Image

2 run ./install_image_imx8.sh script to generate signed Image

2.1 clean the build directory

# ./install_image_imx8.sh -c

2.2 build signing tools and sign Image

# ./install_image_imx8.sh -m sp2imx8mp

NOTE: You may need to install extra library packages to successfully build all
      the required components. i.e. cst

2.3 to re-use your existing PKI keys/crts to sign flash.bin.

# rm -fr build_fw_imx8/release/keys/*
# rm -fr build_fw_imx8/release/crts/*
# cp -fr <YOUR KEYS>/* build_fw_imx8/release/keys/
# cp -fr <YOUR CRTS>/* build_fw_imx8/release/crts/

remove the previous signed Image

# rm -fr build_fw_imx8/Image* build_fw_imx8/ivt*

then run the script again

# ./install_image_imx8.sh -m sp2imx8mp

The signed kernel image is located at build_fw_imx8/Image.signed

